course: dictionary
lesson: 2274
title: Words of belief
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A creed is a short statement of what someone believes. In church, people say the creed together, so everyone hears the same words of belief. Look at the words around creed: «In church, Christians stand and say the Creed» tells you it is said during a service.
explain: Context helps you find the meaning. «People of every race and creed» means people of every religion and belief. The words every race show that creed is not only about church; it means any set of beliefs a person holds.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. «The Apostles' Creed and the Nicene Creed are short statements of belief said together in church.» If you put in "short statements of belief", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: A creed can also be a set of principles that someone lives by. If a person says, "My creed is to always be kind," they are telling you the rule they follow. When you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: A creed is a short statement of the main things a religion believes.
fact: The Apostles' Creed and the Nicene Creed are said together in many churches.
fact: Creed can also mean any set of beliefs or principles someone lives by.
fact: Useful phrases: «say the creed» and «of every creed».
exercise: «The Apostles' Creed and the Nicene Creed are short statements of belief said together in church.» Where are these creeds said? | On the bus | *In many churches | At school during maths | At the football ground
exercise: «People of every race and creed» are welcome here. What does creed mean in this sentence? | A type of food | *Religion or belief | A school subject | A kind of song
exercise: In a church service, what do people often say together? | A weather report | A football chant | A shopping list | *A short creed
test: A creed is best described as | A kind of church building | A type of music | A school trip | *A short statement of what a religion believes
test: Sam says, "My creed is to always tell the truth." What does creed mean here? | A map of the church | *A set of principles someone lives by | A prayer for the sick | A holiday
exam: Which statement about creed is true? | Only fish can have a creed | *It can mean a short statement of belief, or a set of principles someone lives by | A creed is always a song | It means the same as a school timetable
